# Known declaration property: an anonymous function has its exact finite-sequence signature.
# Formerly required a definition route at a higher search ceiling:
# fn(k closed_range(1, 3)) R {0} $in finite_seq(R, 3)
# Run: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/atomic/by_known_special_property/anonymous_fn_in_finite_seq.lit
# Boundary: complete domain and return signature only; no aliases or coercion.
# Wrong domain, wrong return signature and undefined body controls are Rust tests.

fn(k closed_range(1, 3)) R {0} $in finite_seq(R, 3)
fn(j closed_range(1, 0)) R {0} $in finite_seq(R, 0)

claim:
    ? forall n N, value R:
        fn(index closed_range(1, n)) R {value} $in finite_seq(R, n)
